{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/568218-are-demons-immune-to-reality-changes-made-by-angelic-covers","id":568218,"title":"Are demons immune to reality changes made by angelic covers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-25T12:14:30-07:00","id":568218,"title":"Are demons immune to reality changes made by angelic covers?","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Normally angels are created with and/or are given a cover. Suddenly, a new employee works at a company with people thinking he was there already for years, or someone has a new cousin popping up with them thinking he already lived in the house the whole time.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">But how is it with demons involved? Are they also prone to these reality changes by the God Machine (meaning vulnerable) OR do they wake up and go to breakfast and blink, &quot;Um, who the hell is this guy sitting beside sis at the table? Cousin? What cousin? I don't have a cousin -- you don't even have a brother. MOM!&quot; (the one speaking is the demon)</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T14:32:44-07:00","id":568388,"title":"","content":"I'd say they should be immune, but I don't have any actual book references to back that up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T07:55:37-07:00","id":569204,"title":"","content":"In general, I would go with the rules as described under Pacts. Pacts tend to be the number one method that the Unchained make Cover/Infrastructure changes. <br /> <br /> The rule of thumb, if I recall correctly, is that only those who are signed on the pact notice the changes. So, a demon who's indirectly affected by a change would, in fact, think he's sitting next to a cousin he's never had before. <br /> <br /> If it was the work of the God Machine, though, there'd be traces of aether left behind, which would prompt investigation, would lead to plot in an espionage manner, which the game is all about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T19:55:26-07:00","id":569854,"title":"","content":"I'd say no.<br /> <br /> On page 183 of DtD:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The methods of magical occlusion the God-Machine uses to mask its works from mortal eyes do not function against the Unchained. </div> </div> </div>That said, the G-M can upend the physical circumstances of a Demon's life, rewriting, removing or erasing associated mortals (friends, family members, co-workers, etc.) with or without the G-M realizing that an Unchained is caught in the rewrite. Rearranging reality, <i>Dark City</i> or <i>Matrix</i> style is within the G-m's purview. The challenge for the demon is coming home to find an entirely new person where his or her spouse of five years used to be, and having to pretend <i>nothing has changed</i>. Acting a suspicious fashion could trigger a Compromise or alert servants of the G-M to come investigate.<br /> <br /> Since the Demon isn't connected to the G-M, they don't get the 'update files' of the new, changed history, and will need to bluff the gaps in memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}